## Made
I managed to spend some actual time on code this month!
* A good chunk of time was spent on my dotfiles, both to tweak my [jj](https://github.com/jj-vcs/jj) workflow (megamerge
ftw) and because I've been messing with [glide](https://github.com/glide-browser/glide) as
my browser on my work computer, which has been a good time (and I appreciate that it's a
firefox fork instead of chromium).
* I also did some work on [thoth](https://codeberg.org/garrettm/thoth) this month, which
is slowly evolving into my "gimme a summary of whatever things of note happened within X
timeframe" app.
* I did work on the game project I've mentioned before, but progress there has definitely
slowed. That's ok though! I'm enjoying sharpening my `zig` skills with other stuff in the
meantime.

# Stuff I Didn't Do
* Yet again, the secret game project had little to no progress, nor did the short story
I'm writing. But in (good?) news, I've started a *second* short story project because in
the [eternal words of Pip](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dLXeL4HbPr4), we've had one
writing project yes, but what about second writing project?
* I didn't run as much as I intended to, but I did at least start getting *consistent*
again, which I consider more important anyways. Slowly but surely!

# Stuff I'm Gonna Do in May
* The biggest thing I want to try this month is completely avoiding HackerNews. Though I
do find lots of interesting stuff on there, and often learn a lot, recently it's mostly
just been article after article that depresses me more than anything else. I think taking
a breather to just enjoy tech again myself will be good (and it also means I can focus on
curating my RSS feeds, which is a fun bonus background project).
* This is a very small/easy one, but I also would really like to do one of my long runs
this month in another part of the Netherlands. I've had a go-to handful of paths for the
entire 2.5 years I've lived here, and I'm starting to feel the boredom on most of them.
Taking a train to somewhere across the country offers the ability to run in a quieter
place, and maybe even toss in a couple hills. I think this may come towards the end of the
month since I don't really want to do it for anything under 20k, but thankfully I have a
22k lined up for the second to last week of May. Unsure where I'm gonna go yet, but it
should be fun!
